    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0726" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v10/pg694"/>

                <head>259. Memorandum From the Deputy Assistant Secretary of State for Economic
                    Affairs (Kalijarvi) to the
                        Secretary of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d259-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June 26,
                        1957</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Crude Oil Imports in Relation to National Security</item>
                </list>
                <p>At your request we have prepared the attached memorandum which summarizes our
                    conclusions and recommendations for the Department’s position on the crude oil
                    imports problem as related to national security. An underlying memorandum
                    providing the details is in preparation and will reach you shortly.</p>



                <xi:include href="d259-a1.xml" xpointer="d259-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d259-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d259-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 411.006/6–2657. Confidential. Drafted
                    by Beckner and concurred in by L, ARA, EUR, FE, and NEA.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
